const patch = "*** Begin Patch
*** Add File: /work/context/scenarios/SCN-002.md
+Scenario ID: SCN-002
+Title: Reuse an existing bookmark when the same address is saved again
+Type: Edge Case
+Approval status: approved
+Approval session: SESSION-001
+Approval cycle: 1
+
+## Approved behaviour
+When a person submits the exact web address of an existing bookmark, the app does not prepare or create a second copy. It announces that the bookmark is already in the library and opens the existing bookmark's current title and description for editing. Updating it changes that existing entry and confirms the exact updated values with wording that distinguishes an update from a newly saved bookmark.
+
+## Gherkin
+Feature: Avoid duplicate bookmarks
+
+  Scenario: Open an exact duplicate for editing
+    Given a bookmark already exists for a web address
+    When the user submits that exact web address to save it again
+    Then the app states that it is already in the library
+    And the existing bookmark's title and description are opened for editing
+    And no new bookmark is created
+
+  Scenario: Update the bookmark reached through duplicate detection
+    Given an existing bookmark was opened after its web address was submitted again
+    When the user changes its title and updates the bookmark
+    Then the existing bookmark contains the changed title
+    And no new bookmark is created
+    And the confirmation identifies the action as an update and displays the changed value
+
+## Assumptions
+- Duplicate detection in this scenario covers the exact same web address.
+- The existing bookmark is opened directly in editing mode.
+
+## Related scenarios
+- SCN-001
*** Update File: /work/context/scenarios-index.md
@@
